{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b427709c-bd02-41a9-b8a9-24b4e830292a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f54bd27131f5d7f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9008-0aci08zw/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9008-E001.md","content":"# Consolidate enterprise feedback and set the administration usability direction\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the two unknowns that block all configuration and\nintegration work in the strategy. The problem statement records that enterprise account\nfeedback \"arrived through different channels and has not been consolidated\" and is\n\"partially contradictory\". This investigation consolidates that feedback into a single\nrecord, decides a precedence policy for conflicting requirements, and produces a decision\nrecord that (a) selects the direction for the administration requirement — simplifying\nthe exposed configuration surface, adding fine-grained per-project controls, or a layered\ncombination — and (b) names the concrete enterprise tools the integration requirement\nrefers to. The decision record is the input from which the follow-up implementation\ndecomposition is performed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Consolidate all enterprise account feedback referenced by the strategy (field team\n  reports, strategic account channels) into a single record in which every requirement is\n  traceable to its source account(s) and channel.\n- Define a precedence policy for conflicting feedback (which accounts' input carries more\n  weight, and on what basis) and apply it to the HLR-1 conflict: one account wants fewer\n  exposed configuration options, another wants more fine-grained per-project controls.\n- Select exactly one HLR-1 direction: simplification, fine-grained per-project controls,\n  or a layered resolution (curated defaults with opt-in advanced controls). Record the\n  rationale and which conditional implementation plan the selection activates.\n- Identify and name the specific enterprise tools behind the integration requirement\n  (HLR-3), with per-tool rationale drawn from the consolidated feedback; if the feedback\n  contains no tool names, record that finding explicitly and recommend an escalation path\n  (e.g. a structured account survey).\n- Annotate every decision with the downstream work it enables or gates, so a follow-up\n  decomposition can be performed directly from the decision record.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A consolidated feedback record exists that merges every feedback channel referenced by\n  the strategy, with each requirement traceable to its source account(s).\n- The decision record states an explicit precedence policy and applies it to the HLR-1\n  conflict, selecting exactly one of: simplification, fine-grained per-project controls,\n  or layered resolution.\n- The decision record names the concrete enterprise tools for the integration\n  requirement, or documents that no tools could be identified and defines the escalation\n  path.\n- The decision record is reviewed and accepted by product management.\n- Every decision is annotated with the downstream work it gates.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1** (administration should be simpler): resolves the contradictory requirement\n  and selects the implementation direction.\n- **HLR-3** (integrate better with existing enterprise tooling): identifies the concrete\n  tool targets the requirement refers to.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":48363,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9eb016f57a34e3f4","agent_id":"a0cdb5112fc0036ce","session_id":"98e9d94a-7db9-4011-b4e9-ddd4548bd187","uuid":"35dbd09f-e134-4bce-b9a5-50b8f3f3a592","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:00:51.022Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9008"}
