{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b427709c-bd02-41a9-b8a9-24b4e830292a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1ecab5e100c51a1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9008-0aci08zw/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9008-E002.md","content":"# Define data scientist onboarding scope and establish the current-state baseline\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the unknown blocking the onboarding requirement (HLR-2):\n\"onboarding a new data scientist should take less than a day\" is stated without defining\nwhat onboarding includes or where the day is currently spent. The investigation produces\n(a) a ratified definition of what onboarding covers, (b) a current-state analysis of the\nonboarding journey, and (c) a baseline (or a measurement plan) for where time is spent\ntoday, so the one-day target becomes measurable and the improvement work can be\ndecomposed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Propose, and obtain product ratification of, a definition of \"data scientist\n  onboarding\" that states which facets it covers — the strategy enumerates the candidates:\n  cluster access, project setup, first workbench, first deployed model.\n- Produce a current-state analysis of each covered facet's path as it exists today\n  (project creation in the console, workbench spawning and image selection, model serving\n  enablement), with each step cited to public documentation or component source.\n- Establish where onboarding time is currently spent: extract a baseline from existing\n  telemetry or usage data where available, and where no data exists, define the\n  measurement method (instrumentation or structured user research) that will produce it.\n- Compare the current state against the \"less than a day\" target and identify the largest\n  quantified friction points.\n- Recommend which friction points to address, as the input for the follow-up\n  implementation decomposition.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A written onboarding definition exists, approved by product management, that\n  enumerates exactly which facets (cluster access, project setup, first workbench, first\n  deployed model) onboarding covers.\n- The current-state onboarding path is documented step by step, with each step cited to\n  documentation or component source.\n- A time baseline for the defined onboarding path exists, or — where no data is\n  available — a defined measurement method with the data source it requires.\n- A gap summary against the one-day target identifies the largest friction points in\n  measurable terms.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2** (onboarding a new data scientist should take less than a day): defines the\n  scope of \"onboarding\" and establishes the measurement baseline the target requires.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":48363,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9eb016f57a34e3f4","agent_id":"a0cdb5112fc0036ce","session_id":"98e9d94a-7db9-4011-b4e9-ddd4548bd187","uuid":"4fd9843e-8906-4dfc-ae11-e4be5d7f83bb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:01:03.212Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9008"}
