{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-027231f6-bf9c-431e-96a1-584a7ef8e2a7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9203a958a825f8e4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9008-0aci08zw/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9008-BRANCH-A-E004.md","content":"# Streamline the administration configuration surface\n\n## Description\n\nConditional implementation plan, active only if the enterprise feedback investigation\nselects the simplification direction for the administration requirement (the account\nfeedback calling for fewer exposed configuration options takes precedence). This epic\nreduces the number of administration configuration options exposed to administrators in\nthe RHOAI Dashboard, replacing removed knobs with curated defaults, with the specific\noption set defined by the investigation's decision record.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Reduce the set of administration configuration options exposed in the Dashboard\n  administration surface, per the option list in the investigation decision record. The\n  configuration surface is the Dashboard admin settings backed by the OdhDashboardConfig\n  custom resource, as documented in the RHOAI architecture context.\n- Provide curated defaults for every removed or hidden option that preserve current\n  behavior for existing deployments.\n- Make the changed configuration surface reversible via a feature flag or equivalent\n  rollback mechanism, since this modifies an existing capability.\n- Update captions, references, and settings documentation that fall out of the same\n  change (no new content authored).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The count of exposed administration configuration options matches the reduced set\n  defined in the investigation decision record.\n- Deployments that used the previous defaults exhibit unchanged behavior after the\n  change (defaults preserve prior outcomes).\n- The changed surface is reversible via a feature flag or documented rollback path.\n- Every removed option has a documented default value, and existing administrator\n  workflows are regression-tested against the reduced surface.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1** (administration should be simpler): implements the simplification direction —\n  fewer exposed configuration options with curated defaults.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50306,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9eb016f57a34e3f4","agent_id":"a0cdb5112fc0036ce","session_id":"98e9d94a-7db9-4011-b4e9-ddd4548bd187","uuid":"5d8304e7-5aef-403d-8197-9a4cb9a03aec","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:01:24.490Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9008"}
