{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-027231f6-bf9c-431e-96a1-584a7ef8e2a7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8699fa047ecc7ace","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9008-0aci08zw/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9008-BRANCH-B-E004.md","content":"# Add fine-grained per-project administration controls\n\n## Description\n\nConditional implementation plan, active only if the enterprise feedback investigation\nselects the fine-grained direction for the administration requirement (the account\nfeedback calling for more per-project controls takes precedence). This epic adds\nper-project granularity to RHOAI administration controls in the Dashboard, with the\nspecific control set defined by the investigation's decision record.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add per-project administration controls to the Dashboard administration surface, per\n  the control list in the investigation decision record. The existing configuration\n  surface (Dashboard admin settings backed by the OdhDashboardConfig custom resource, and\n  the per-workbench override pattern used for culling settings) is the documented\n  foundation; the specific mechanism is an implementation decision for the team.\n- Preserve platform-wide defaults wherever no per-project override is set, so existing\n  deployments are unaffected until an administrator opts in.\n- Document the new control surface and the precedence order between platform-wide\n  defaults and per-project overrides.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Per-project administration controls operate as defined in the investigation decision\n  record, and a per-project override takes precedence over the platform-wide default for\n  the affected project only.\n- Projects without an override behave identically to the current platform-wide defaults.\n- The precedence rules and available controls are documented.\n- Existing platform-wide administration workflows are regression-tested and unaffected\n  where no override exists.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1** (administration should be simpler): implements the fine-grained direction —\n  more granular per-project administration controls.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50306,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9eb016f57a34e3f4","agent_id":"a0cdb5112fc0036ce","session_id":"98e9d94a-7db9-4011-b4e9-ddd4548bd187","uuid":"1e3882be-c0e3-4be6-bf19-b765fa1c964e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:01:32.513Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9008"}
