istration and configuration practices, data scientist\n50\t  onboarding practices, and integration with enterprise tooling.\n51\t- Draft the whitepaper through the Red Hat docs content process, grounded in the\n52\t  investigation decision records (consolidated feedback, selected administration\n53\t  direction, named integration targets, onboarding definition and baseline).\n54\t- Validate the draft for technical accuracy against the RHOAI architecture context for\n55\t  the affected components (Dashboard, Notebooks) and the investigation findings.\n56\t- Publish the whitepaper through the designated Red Hat content channel.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- A content outline exists covering administration, onboarding, and enterprise\n61\t  integration practices, and is agreed with the strategy owner.\n62\t- The draft is technically reviewed for accuracy against the investigation decision\n63\t  records and the RHOAI architecture context (Dashboard and Notebooks component\n64\t  documentation); every product claim in the draft traces to a reviewed source.\n65\t- The whitepaper is published in the designated Red Hat content channel.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- **HLR-4** (publish a whitepaper describing enterprise usability best practices on\n70\t  RHOAI): direct, complete coverage.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b305912d97c92d7","agent_id":"a6d2ecbd0d01bdd6b","session_id":"98e9d94a-7db9-4011-b4e9-ddd4548bd187","uuid":"d9eb249d-b08b-4c0a-a3cc-14b5f24886e9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:15:04.561Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9350111cb02cb6e0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9008 decomposition"}
