{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8659b6569ffebc09","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-E003\n3\ttitle: Author and publish the RHOAI enterprise usability whitepaper\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: RHOAI Documentation\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9008-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9008-E002\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9008-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the enterprise feedback investigation changes direction or\n17\t    finds no integration targets, the whitepaper outline is re-scoped to the resolved\n18\t    direction. If the onboarding scope investigation redefines what onboarding covers\n19\t    or overturns the current-state baseline, the onboarding-practices section is re-scoped\n20\t    the same way. The draft is revised against the final decision records from both\n21\t    investigations before publication.\n22\tai_signals:\n23\t  change_specificity: 0\n24\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n25\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n26\t  existing_foundation: 0\n27\t  open_questions: -1\n28\t  external_dependency: 1\n29\t  human_process_gates: -1\n30\t  repo_access: 1\n31\t  architecture_claims: 1\n32\tinvestigation_signals: null\n33\tai_implementability: Medium\n34\tai_implementability_score: 1\n35\tjira_key: null\n36\tbranch: null\n37\t---\n38\t# Author and publish the RHOAI enterprise usability whitepaper\n39\t\n40\t## Description\n41\t\n42\tThis epic delivers the strategy's documentation requirement (HLR-4): a published\n43\twhitepaper describing enterprise usability best practices on RHOAI. The content draws on\n44\tthe resolved enterprise usability direction (administration configuration practices,\n45\tidentified integration targets) and the onboarding definition and baseline produced by\n46\tthe upstream investigations, and is validated for technical accuracy against the RHOAI\n47\tarchitecture context.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Content outline for the whitepaper covering enterprise usability best practices on\n52\t  RHOAI across three areas: administration and configuration practices, data scientist\n53\t  onboarding practices, and integration with enterprise tooling.\n54\t- Draft the whitepaper through the Red Hat docs content process, grounded in the\n55\t  investigation decision records (consolidated feedback, selected administration\n56\t  direction, named integration targets, onboarding definition and baseline).\n57\t- Validate the draft for technical accuracy against the RHOAI architecture context for\n58\t  the affected components (Dashboard, Notebooks) and the investigation findings.\n59\t- Publish the whitepaper through the designated Red Hat content channel.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- A content outline exists covering administration, onboarding, and enterprise\n64\t  integration practices, and is agreed with the strategy owner.\n65\t- The draft is technically reviewed for accuracy against the investigation decision\n66\t  records and the RHOAI architecture context (Dashboard and Notebooks component\n67\t  documentation); every product claim in the draft traces to a reviewed source.\n68\t- The whitepaper is published in the designated Red Hat content channel.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- **HLR-4** (publish a whitepaper describing enterprise usability best practices on\n73\t  RHOAI): direct, complete coverage.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b305912d97c92d7","agent_id":"a6d2ecbd0d01bdd6b","session_id":"98e9d94a-7db9-4011-b4e9-ddd4548bd187","uuid":"497fbc57-250e-4945-a923-674470a92314","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:16:34.943Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8659b6569ffebc09","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTR