{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99dfa7322412371b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\n3\tepic_count: 3\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9008 (Make RHOAI more usable for enterprise teams)\n11\t\n12\t## Triage Outcome\n13\t\n14\tNeither Step 0 check fires; full decomposition was performed.\n15\t\n16\t- **Below-threshold**: does not apply. The strategy contains genuine unknowns — all three\n17\t  open questions (feedback precedence for HLR-1, onboarding scope for HLR-2, target tools\n18\t  for HLR-3) would change which epics exist or what they do. The scope also spans multiple\n19\t  distinct work streams (administration configuration, onboarding, enterprise integrations,\n20\t  and a whitepaper) across two components (Dashboard, Notebooks).\n21\t- **Docs-only**: does not apply. Dashboard and Notebooks are code components.\n22\t\n23\t## Step 1 — Parse Results and Missing Sections\n24\t\n25\tParsed: High-Level Requirements (HLR-1..4), Affected Components (Dashboard, Notebooks),\n26\tOut of Scope (nothing scoped out), Open Questions (3).\n27\t\n28\t**Missing strategy sections** (health warnings, decomposition proceeded with available data):\n29\tImpacted Teams table, Dependencies table, Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then),\n30\tNon-Functional Requirements, Staff Engineer Input, Technical Approach.\n31\t\n32\t## Step 1.5 — Staff Engineer Input\n33\t\n34\tNo Staff Engineer Input section exists in the strategy; no overrides to log.\n35\t\n36\t## Component Mapping\n37\t\n38\tBoth affected components (Dashboard, Notebooks) exist in\n39\t`.context/architecture-context/` (in platform, Konflux-onboarded, GA) — no onboarding\n40\tchain needed. Owning teams were taken from the architecture context because the strategy\n41\thas no Impacted Teams table:\n42\t\n43\t| Epic | Canonical component | Team | Note |\n44\t|------|--------------------|------|------|\n45\t| E001 | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard | Span: consolidation covers all feedback (Dashboard + Notebooks surfaces); Dashboard assigned as the contested HLR-1 administration surface (OdhDashboardConfig per dashboard.md) |\n46\t| E002 | Notebooks | Workbenches | Span: onboarding journey crosses Dashboard (project setup, spawn UI) and Notebooks (workbench); Notebooks assigned as the core data-scientist onboarding artifact |\n47\t| E003 | Documentation | RHOAI Documentation | Team assumed — no team information exists in the strategy |\n48\t| BRANCH-A/B/C-E004 | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard | HLR-1 implementation surface is the Dashboard administration configuration |\n49\t\n50\t## Epic List\n51\t\n52\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n53\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n54\t| E001 | Consolidate enterprise feedback and set the administration usability direction | Investigation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n55\t| E002 | Define data scientist onboarding scope and establish the current-state baseline | Investigation | Workbenches | P1 |\n56\t| E003 | Author and publish the RHOAI enterprise usability whitepaper | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P2 |\n57\t| BRANCH-A-E004 | Streamline the administration configuration surface (conditional) | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n58\t| BRANCH-B-E004 | Add fine-grained per-project administration controls (conditional) | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n59\t| BRANCH-C-E004 | Implement layered administration defaults with opt-in advanced controls (conditional) | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n60\t\n61\t`epic_count` counts the 3 main-plan epics; the 3 branch epics are conditional plan\n62\tdocuments attached to E001, not standalone Jira issues.\n63\t\n64\t## Dependency DAG\n65\t\n66\tMain plan:\n67\t\n68\t```mermaid\n69\tgraph TD\n70\t    E001[\"E001 Consolidate feedback / set direction (Investigation)\"]\n71\t    E002[\"E002 Define onboarding scope + baseline (Investigation)\"]\n72\t    E003[\"E003 Enterprise usability whitepaper (docs-authoring)\"]\n73\t    E001 --> E003\n74\t    E002 --> E003\n75\t```\n76\t\n77\tConditional branches selected by the E001 outcome for HLR-1 (bounded, 3 outcomes):\n78\t\n79\t```mermaid\n80\tgraph TD\n81\t    E001[\"E001 Investigation\"]\n82\t    BA[\"BRANCH-A-E004 Streamline config surface\"]\n83\t    BB[\"BRANCH-B-E004 Fine-grained per-project controls\"]\n84\t    BC[\"BRANCH-C-E004 Layered defaults + advanced controls\"]\n85\t    E001 -. selects one .-> BA\n86\t    E001 -. selects one .-> BB\n87\t    E001 -. selects one .-> BC\n88\t```\n89\t\n90\t## DAG Justification\n91\t\n92\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n93\t|------|------|-----------|\n94\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 3, Rule 11 | The whitepaper's content (which usability practices to describe) is defined by the investigation outcomes; docs-authoring is sequenced after the available upstream work. Gate type: `rewrite` (outcome changes content, not existence) — recorded as `gated_by` on E003 |\n95\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 3, Rule 11 | Onboarding findings are a primary input to the onboarding-practices section of the whitepaper. Same `rewrite` gate character as E001, but `gated_by` is single-valued in the schema, so only the primary gate (E001) is recorded there; E002's failure impact is covered explicitly in E003's `gate_failure_impact` fallback |\n96\t| E001 → BRANCH-A/B/C-E004 | Rule 3 | Bounded outcomes (≤3) → conditional decomposition branches. Each branch exists only under its outcome; gate type `remove` for every branch (mutually exclusive alternatives) |\n97\t| E001 ∥ E002 | — | Independent unknowns resolved by different experiments (feedback consolidation vs onboarding current-state analysis); no edge |\n98\t\n99\t## Investigation Scoping Decisions\n100\t\n101\t- **Open question 1 (feedback precedence, HLR-1) and open question 3 (which enterprise\n102\t  tools