{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82b5fa1e33e6372b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-BRANCH-C-E004\n3\ttitle: Implement layered administration defaults with opt-in advanced controls\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: C\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9008-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9008-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: This epic exists only if the enterprise feedback investigation\n16\t    selects the layered resolution (curated defaults plus opt-in advanced controls).\n17\t    If a single direction is selected instead, this epic is removed in favor of the\n18\t    branch matching that outcome.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 4\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Implement layered administration defaults with opt-in advanced controls\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tConditional implementation plan, active only if the enterprise feedback investigation\n40\tselects the layered resolution for the administration requirement (both accounts' needs\n41\tare met: a simple default experience plus opt-in fine-grained control). This epic\n42\tintroduces curated defaults that hide advanced administration options behind an opt-in\n43\tsurface in the RHOAI Dashboard, so administrators see fewer knobs by default while\n44\tretaining full per-project control when needed. The specific option and control sets are\n45\tdefined by the investigation's decision record.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Implement a default administration view in the Dashboard that exposes only the curated\n50\t  set of options defined in the investigation decision record, backed by the OdhDashboardConfig\n51\t  configuration surface documented in the RHOAI architecture context.\n52\t- Implement an opt-in advanced surface exposing the fine-grained per-project controls\n53\t  defined in the decision record, available to administrators who need them.\n54\t- Make the layered presentation reversible via a feature flag or equivalent rollback\n55\t  mechanism, since this modifies an existing capability.\n56\t- Document the default view, the advanced surface, and the precedence between curated\n57\t  defaults, platform-wide settings, and per-project overrides.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- The default administration view exposes exactly the curated option set from the\n62\t  decision record; the advanced controls are hidden until opted into.\n63\t- Opting in exposes the full fine-grained control set, and per-project overrides take\n64\t  precedence over curated defaults for the affected project only.\n65\t- Deployments that do not opt in behave as if only the curated defaults exist (no\n66\t  behavior change for existing default configurations).\n67\t- The layered presentation is reversible via a feature flag or documented rollback path.\n68\t- The default view, advanced surface, and precedence rules are documented.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- **HLR-1** (administration should be simpler): implements the layered resolution —\n73\t  curated defaults satisfying the \"fewer knobs\" account, with opt-in per-project controls\n74\t  satisfying the fine-grained account.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0e45f1a5d9d5b82","agent_id":"a00317b63ea50ba62","session_id":"98e9d94a-7db9-4011-b4e9-ddd4548bd187","uuid":"a773765e-b7fa-4002-9769-395fecfe0b09","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:18:28.315Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-82b5fa1e33e6372b","p